@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4">
                <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
                <p class="text-muted">
                    This notice explains what information SmartElderlyCare collects, why we
                    collect it, and how we protect it.
                </p>

                <h4 class="mt-4">1. Purpose of the system</h4>
                <p>
                    SmartElderlyCare helps health facilities, Village Health Workers (VHWs) and the
                    Health Information Unit (HIU) monitor the health and welfare of elderly patients
                    between clinic visits.
                </p>

                <h4 class="mt-4">2. Information we collect</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Patient details:</strong> name, date of birth, gender, national ID,
                        address, phone, medical condition, chronic care programme, emergency contact.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Vital signs:</strong> temperature, blood pressure, pulse, respiration,
                        oxygen saturation, blood glucose, weight.
                    </li>
                    <li>Facility visit records, VHW welfare checks, and alerts.</li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Staff account details:</strong> display name, email, phone, role,
                        login activity.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="mt-4">3. How the information is used</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>To check readings against safe thresholds and raise alerts.</li>
                    <li>To show patient history and risk level to authorised staff.</li>
                    <li>To prepare monthly DHIS2 indicator reports and district reports.</li>
                    <li>Not used for advertising and not sold to any third party.</li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="mt-4">4. Who can see the information</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Access depends on the user role (Administrator, Nurse, Facility Nurse, VHW,
                        Records Staff, HIU Clerk, DHIO Admin, DMO, Family).
                    </li>
                    <li>Family members see only the patient they are linked to.</li>
                    <li>
                        Reports sent to DHIS2 contain aggregated indicators, not individual patient
                        details.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="mt-4">5. How the information is protected</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Passwords are stored in hashed form and never shown in plain text.</li>
                    <li>
                        Role-based access control, account lockout after 5 failed logins
                        (15 minutes), and automatic session expiry.
                    </li>
                    <li>Secure cookies and anti-forgery protection on forms.</li>
                    <li>An audit trail records administrative actions (who, what and when).</li>
                    <li>Regular database backups.</li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="mt-4">6. Keeping information</h4>
                <p>
                    Records are kept while the patient is enrolled and as required by Ministry of
                    Health and Child Care rules. Accounts of staff who leave are deactivated.
                </p>

                <h4 class="mt-4">7. Your rights</h4>
                <p>
                    Patients and their families may ask to view or correct their information through
                    the facility or the contact below, in line with the Cyber and Data Protection
                    Act of Zimbabwe.
                </p>

                <h4 class="mt-4">8. Contact</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Email: support@@elderlycare.gov.zw</li>
                    <li>Phone: +263 242 700000, +263 772 000001</li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="mt-4">9. Changes to this notice</h4>
                <p>
                    This notice may be updated as the system grows or as laws change. The date
                    below shows when it was last reviewed.
                </p>

                <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Last updated: 3 October 2026</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
